CORE since 2026-09-23: the interaction no longer reproduces (the second
__invoke_result use resolves; the file has no main, so the translation unit is
checked through --function adjust_float_expressions).
libstdc++-13's __invoke_result/_S_test machinery instantiated TWICE:
first through __umap_hashtable's default template argument
(__cache_default -> __is_nothrow_invocable<hash,int>, at a global
variable's type), then through std::function's _Callable constraint
during a member call's ctor deduction.  The second use fails ("found
no match for symbol 'transform'") ONLY when the first is present --
cvise could remove nothing from the 75 lines, so every piece
(including the seemingly unrelated unordered_map machinery) is
load-bearing: a cached-instance-poisoning interaction, the
"permanently truncated cached instances" family.  Reduced from
CBMC's own adjust_float_expressions.cpp (the instructiont::transform
dog-food family, round 129); the parenthesised-class-tag sub-shape
was already fixed (ed78322744).  g++/clang accept.
